n NATO to withdraw from large parts of Eastern Europe. What this would mean for the security of millions of Europeans — and what lies behind Russia's plan.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Rights court rules Turkey must release jailed lawmaker Atalay</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c97af9b46d907d31c242a3209212a0e58d8c8eae7e1e64b2b313bc49900eebe6</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T15:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/rights-court-rules-turkey-must-release-jailed-lawmaker-atalay/a-79972462--8247972e6110.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/rights-court-rules-turkey-must-release-jailed-lawmaker-atalay/a-79972462?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Court of Human Rights has called for the release of imprisoned elected lawmaker Can Atalay. Atalay has been in prison for almost five years despite rulings from the Turkish Constitutional Court.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nvidia forms national security committee after Huang affair</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bed6e5c5be595ca55a66449c812d9a5d330505fc29e7b715c00a93a01c3fb985</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T14:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nvidia-forms-national-security-committee-after-huang-affair/a-79970447--7d1c93df3ff0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nvidia-forms-national-security-committee-after-huang-affair/a-79970447?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nvidia has created a board-level committee for national security and export control. This follows the resignation of CEO Jensen Huang over extramarital affairs, allegedly including one with a Chinese intelligence asset.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Students' List candidates take seats as Serbian parliament opens</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fdc6f469b5aabe19f3e694e83912a37bfc60c0b708b20083a7da9fc2c7714bbf</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T12:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/students-list-candidates-take-seats-as-serbian-parliament-opens/a-79969166--96de93cfad7f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/students-list-candidates-take-seats-as-serbian-parliament-opens/a-79969166?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Serbia's Student List's candidates have taken their oaths in the inaugural parliament session. As the new majority, they have 90 days to form a government.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Klopp and Wirtz offer glimpse of bright German future</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b358b03ee94e66b9ffffb0ef526dccbc70109ffc5af570840ee423e3f04e67fb</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T11:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/klopp-and-wirtz-offer-glimpse-of-bright-german-future/a-79968184--a5059b3200c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/klopp-and-wirtz-offer-glimpse-of-bright-german-future/a-79968184?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's fall from grace in recent years has seen the team drift away from the fans. But Monday's drubbing of the Netherlands and the impact of Jürgen Klopp, Florian Wirtz and emerging youngsters offers hope.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Could the Airbus €3 billion loan row reignite a US-EU trade dispute?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bf18014d48c649cabd8bdfd1cf4ab511d5438163078047d42026f6015b0fce62</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T11:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/could-the-airbus-_3-billion-loan-row-reignite-a-us-eu-trade-dispute/a-79943075--30f362f3b820.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/could-the-airbus-€3-billion-loan-row-reignite-a-us-eu-trade-dispute/a-79943075?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US says a record €3 billion financing package for Airbus may conflict with a transatlantic aircraft-subsidy truce. EU officials insist the funding complies with market-based rules.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Plans for Rwanda migrant hub come under fire</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f4df4413d99d271b45423510caf13fb970116276caf68fcf459776edc972fd2</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T10:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-plans-for-rwanda-migrant-hub-come-under-fire/live-79965639--9c6685ac3d74.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-plans-for-rwanda-migrant-hub-come-under-fire/live-79965639?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Human rights groups have slammed plans by Germany and four other EU states to send rejected asylum seekers to Rwanda. In other news, business start-ups in Germany are on track to reach the highest level since 2015.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France's Philippe Diallo to challenge Infantino for FIFA presidency</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2871b69e7852dd24ef6eebf7cd00448e939ba49c3ef1af11be0f83f7fa1e529d</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T20:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-s-philippe-diallo-to-challenge-infantino-for-fifa-presidency/a-79962843--6fe08ae5c0bf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-s-philippe-diallo-to-challenge-infantino-for-fifa-presidency/a-79962843?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Philippe Diallo is the second candidate to stand against incumbent Gianni Infantino. He is backed by European football's governing body UEFA, known to be critical of Infantino.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>NASA's Voyager 1 reaches a light-day away from Earth</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a9fd2146fcf45ed39a88d60891792fc7cd5bc7668bab2be2dda3b9564b624bc</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T17:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nasa-s-voyager-1-reaches-a-light-day-away-from-earth/a-79961817--190e9087abf2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nasa-s-voyager-1-reaches-a-light-day-away-from-earth/a-79961817?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">When just saying 'hello' takes a two-day round trip, you're a light-day, or 26 billion kilometers, from Earth. Only one human-made object has ever traveled that far — and its journey into interstellar space continues.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>What has changed in James Bond films over the decades</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:49ad6c3636efa68b599901590663bdb97480647ea647f8fe4bb1bfbc4d0890f1</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T17:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-has-changed-in-james-bond-films-over-the-decades/a-63332001--7d894a9cd4fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-has-changed-in-james-bond-films-over-the-decades/a-63332001?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In 1962, a martini-drinking womanizer saved the world for the first time in "Dr. No." As Robert Pattinson takes on the role of 007, here's how the films evolved.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>The AfD and neo-Nazi networks: How close are the connections?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ba719097a841d6ad90b1c24d0dc23522ef6104abe84740912567cd0858d83564</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T16:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-afd-and-neo-nazi-networks-how-close-are-the-connections/a-79961920--fb16f5d74381.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-afd-and-neo-nazi-networks-how-close-are-the-connections/a-79961920?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Alternative for Germany party (AfD) has become a focal point for the far right. Many of its members and staff have ties to ethnonationalist or neo-Nazi organizations.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>COP31 draft deal calls for 'immediate' shift away from fossil fuels</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:77c30bb9416e175255f3f09e706b2dd5c0b3780abaf9e6a3643fe05052f562d8</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T14:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cop31-draft-deal-calls-for-immediate-shift-away-from-fossil-fuels/a-79960705--2a7f1bfc2c85.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cop31-draft-deal-calls-for-immediate-shift-away-from-fossil-fuels/a-79960705?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The preliminary agreement at UN climate talks in Turkey calls for a rapid reduction of planet-warming emissions and at least $120 billion to help countries adapt to climate change.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Klopp wants Infantino out as FIFA candidate deadline looms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4ebf65beef74c46a0e2cba7b30bf1b9f7e12431c7fcfa4627083004bf5f3aa46</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T11:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/klopp-wants-infantino-out-as-fifa-candidate-deadline-looms/a-79958229--458d3356c9f8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/klopp-wants-infantino-out-as-fifa-candidate-deadline-looms/a-79958229?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany coach Jürgen Klopp has joined the chorus of football figures critical of FIFA President Gianni Infantino. But with time running out, there are few who seem willing to run against him.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Merz, Söder aim to revisit electricity tax cut</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02329d5db47c92c14d1795feaec484ce9c00a92eba968149637523e20736867f</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T08:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-s_der-aim-to-revisit-electricity-tax-cut/live-79954869--6bc156ed2286.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-söder-aim-to-revisit-electricity-tax-cut/live-79954869?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Christian Democrats are in Munich, pushing to revive some tax relief that didn't make it into the budget after talks last week. And Manuela Schwesig faces a vote on a new term as regional leader. Follow DW.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Can a 'coalition of the willing' create momentum for a fossil fuel phaseout?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:451290b2e30d1d2f61fd0a6294b336c263936ff64ed640e390dbcbfe66d0c25d</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T08:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-a-coalition-of-the-willing-create-momentum-for-a-fossil-fuel-phaseout/a-79926748--1f05ab68dfcb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-a-coalition-of-the-willing-create-momentum-for-a-fossil-fuel-phaseout/a-79926748?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In April, about 60 countries held an unprecedented meeting in Colombia to work out a plan to slowly quit oil, coal and gas. How influential is this coalition at the COP31 climate summit?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>AI in classrooms: Fighting the great 'dumbing down'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa7833a5524fcee963cddb881abab70db2e98852583967da096706265f4fd5eb</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T07:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ai-in-classrooms-fighting-the-great-dumbing-down/a-79949229--354992b7f6e4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ai-in-classrooms-fighting-the-great-dumbing-down/a-79949229?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Research suggests that students who aren't careful about how they use ChatGPT and other AI tools risk poorer academic outcomes. It's a huge challenge for teachers.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>German economy returns to growth, so why is the country still worried?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4b5e6ff89cb0362b2a22fc2899bc5ab1665eda24c1ecded231fcb0b123fe8845</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T16:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-economy-returns-to-growth-so-why-is-the-country-still-worried/a-79932220--24d2aa1d0aab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-economy-returns-to-growth-so-why-is-the-country-still-worried/a-79932220?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The German economy is growing again, albeit slightly. However, economists warn that without reforms, higher productivity and solid public finances, a loss of prosperity and growing debt threaten future generations.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Despite restrictive abortion laws, Poland's 'Abortomat' — a locker that dispenses abortion pills — helps women who want to end a pregnancy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b9dab51e130b84f738cf9f7ec580bdae7d3e844b56275f21688628401369e73c</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T14:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/polish-activists-face-opposition-as-they-make-abortion-more-accessible/a-79943914--39db4083c558.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/despite-restrictive-abortion-laws-poland-s-abortomat-a-locker-that-dispenses-abortion-pills-helps-women-who-want-to-end-a-pregnancy/a-79943914?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Abortion laws in Poland are very restrictive. Activists there have found a new way to help women wanting to terminate a pregnancy: the "Abortomat," a locker that dispenses abortion pills. But they face fierce opposition.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Germany holds national day of remembrance</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f2d7b22f420b2ee4f2c2cb8f8897cabf926d5bba7c3ac0f8610c470c3e2f25b5</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T07:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-germany-holds-national-day-of-remembrance/live-79947500--7252f2ee958f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-germany-holds-national-day-of-remembrance/live-79947500?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Events were held for "Volkstrauertag," a day commemorating victims of war and oppression. Meanwhile, experts said the country is headed for a budget crisis.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How AI is likely to change Germany's job market</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:38a8956039a7d668826e9d5b9cd7f911173c62f665104e0f39f5b9bd011e09c9</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T05:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-ai-is-likely-to-change-germany-s-job-market/a-79941597--3a5b2bd9406d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-ai-is-likely-to-change-germany-s-job-market/a-79941597?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The scale of the economic disruption caused by AI has led even conservative politicians to talk about universal basic income. Bu