dw.com/en/what-are-fossil-fuels/a-67970540?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">They are in our shampoo bottles, power our cars and heat our homes. But what actually are fossil fuels, and why do they matter?</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Police raid chapters of Gremium MC biker gang</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:48825ddf95394ece3ff115a1f884ac90c2bbe67784ecf2ab7c794aef8fc009d6</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T09:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-police-raid-chapters-of-gremium-mc-biker-gang/live-79926275--65b7228f3ec1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-police-raid-chapters-of-gremium-mc-biker-gang/live-79926275?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police in southwestern Germany launched major early-morning operations against a biker gang. The state of Baden-Württemberg is outlawing three of its chapters. Meanwhile, unions are planning more strikes.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bundeswehr study exposes widespread sexual harassment in German military</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:841cc751d787b2b9084b5c20b359924ad84caf0a9502e3e3c7448123b41356ef</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T08:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bundeswehr-study-exposes-widespread-sexual-harassment-in-german-military/a-79926359--0cec81791758.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bundeswehr-study-exposes-widespread-sexual-harassment-in-german-military/a-79926359?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Sexual misconduct in the Bundeswehr is far more widespread than previously known, with younger women disproportionately affected. Defense Minister Boris Pistorius has called for a policy of "zero tolerance."</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Intelligent women get less help at work, study finds</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0247ab6596a4299f7a2290f89f1588dd5507abd31df17d27d28ae87ad7e8d326</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T07:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/intelligent-women-get-less-help-at-work-study-finds/a-79910881--d3f9551f1647.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/intelligent-women-get-less-help-at-work-study-finds/a-79910881?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Women who scored high on intelligence tests were seen as more hostile by their teammates and got less help, a new study finds. High-scoring men faced no such penalty. Research explains why.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Fears of rising antisemitism in Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b14c5f375330736f6b4789a8696fedb7c1290d71f88ba5e26aefb7818ee9b0ec</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T20:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fears-of-rising-antisemitism-in-europe/a-79921783--20638e7d2425.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fears-of-rising-antisemitism-in-europe/a-79921783?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Holocaust survivor Regina Sluszny commemorates the victims of Auschwitz as Jewish communities across Europe face growing hostility. What does the promise of "Never Again" mean for Jewish life in Europe today?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Why the integration of immigrants in Germany remains a challenge</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0a85540c771f6d92a7c09c3509c0eff32a18464fa888972baa7f6b1380d761c8</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T17:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-the-integration-of-immigrants-in-germany-remains-a-challenge/a-79923241--a319297bc2a0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-the-integration-of-immigrants-in-germany-remains-a-challenge/a-79923241?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Federal Office for Migration and Refugees has released a new Integration Report. It found that while the integration of people with a migrant background is improving, violent youth remain a problem.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Democracy study: One-quarter of Germans want a right-wing authoritarian dictatorship</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6e4063feaa37b95f2344431b1fb4510afe18964b91f3a660da7723ee0e18bced</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T16:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/democracy-study-one-quarter-of-germans-want-a-right-wing-authoritarian-dictatorship/a-79922718--e6377f13d887.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/democracy-study-one-quarter-of-germans-want-a-right-wing-authoritarian-dictatorship/a-79922718?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The far-right AfD's electoral successes point to a new trend in Germany: Prejudice, resentment, and extremism are on the rise. A new study suggests satisfaction with democracy is at a low ebb.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Is AIIB's complaint mechanism failing affected communities?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:29ede6cd734494378a8f4c971c9f497ea709237fa3b817bd1992d64a4a31a4e0</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-aiib-s-complaint-mechanism-failing-affected-communities/a-79919917--1bfa788b7764.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-aiib-s-complaint-mechanism-failing-affected-communities/a-79919917?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank has a grievance redress mechanism for people affected by projects it finances. But those seeking to file a complaint face significant hurdles. Critics say reforms are needed.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Wael Mohya could make German football history at 17</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:73d0619a382e74160b32972aa754da9864d6588d4bfd94febd76083d64af9303</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787--677b2c671ea6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At just 17, Gladbach forward Wael Mohya has earned his first Germany call-up. The dual-national talent has chosen the DFB path for now — and could soon make modern national-team history.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Can global leaders put their money where their mouth is on climate?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:79ae5e70dd20111ec92d71a91dc1a461f976ef52cbcaf1fc5102cc232c29df1f</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T14:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-global-leaders-put-their-money-where-their-mouth-is-on-climate/a-79918744--b2fe82b3dbb0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-global-leaders-put-their-money-where-their-mouth-is-on-climate/a-79918744?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">World leaders warn that geopolitical divisions are distracting from the climate crisis as negotiations focus on clean energy and financing, while Iran calls for compensation for war-related environmental damage.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>DW Science explainer on the default mode network: what your brain does when you aren't focusing on anything, and why it's important.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1cd8bc2d8fdb89df65f8cf6bdf90cadfda7c218a7b38436fb33bb4d9c5c60c6e</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T06:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dw-science-explainer-on-the-default-mode-network-what-your-brain-does-when-you-aren-t-focusing-on-an/a-79908787--cf91bcf53b1d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dw-science-explainer-on-the-default-mode-network-what-your-brain-does-when-you-aren-t-focusing-on-anything-and-why-it-s-important/a-79908787?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Doing nothing might be the ultimate brain hack. When you're bored, the brain goes into default mode network. It's not only healthy for you, but it may also shape the very essence of your identity.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Germany slips in climate protection rankings as other countries make gains</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3aba3bb788085b93e71965ea0533d98eba0ac5e42140035a4904bfd9aaca3d2a</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T06:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-slips-in-climate-protection-rankings-as-other-countries-make-gains/a-79913635--edb7d622928e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-slips-in-climate-protection-rankings-as-other-countries-make-gains/a-79913635?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Record renewable energy growth is driving climate progress in some countries, but Germany and many major emitters are falling behind.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>British counterterrorism police arrest US soldier accused of spying on behalf of Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6e49f5bbe7d79dcb569520ded634a041c0d3a71b660e9c0834d1057844316bee</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T19:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/british-counterterrorism-police-arrest-us-soldier-accused-of-spying-on-behalf-of-russia/a-79913240--5991e0a904a3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/british-counterterrorism-police-arrest-us-soldier-accused-of-spying-on-behalf-of-russia/a-79913240?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A member of the US Army has been arrested near Gloucester in England. Police said he was suspected of espionage activity in connection with Russia. Investigators from the US and UK are involved in the probe.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>UK Privy Council overrules Trinidad and Tobago gay sex law</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:10f240614f2f911e59245f83bd8a86ac1d4b692ff7b5a1dcb50bb3161bac1fda</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T19:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-privy-council-overrules-trinidad-and-tobago-gay-sex-law/a-79912163--f186aba38925.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-privy-council-overrules-trinidad-and-tobago-gay-sex-law/a-79912163?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A London court has overturned a Trinidad and Tobago law criminalizing consensual sexual relations between male same-sex couples. As a result of the colonial legacy, it is the independent country's last court of appeal.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Victims of Nazi war in Poland call on Germany for support</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8b1e897a4f099f4641fa7dfba41d3dfaf41c6a52b7a39cd66075efe1a45e5da4</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T17:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/victims-of-nazi-war-in-poland-call-on-germany-for-support/a-79909311--36756d6320e4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/victims-of-nazi-war-in-poland-call-on-germany-for-support/a-79909311?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">More than 80 years after the end of World War II, Polish victims of the Nazi regime are still waiting for a "humanitarian gesture" from Germany. The 2027 draft budget hasn't left them much hope for possible reparations.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran denies role in fridge hack, France summons ambassador</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:86155543decb5df7bd763d31769a1f93154b7943b5ed4818f32a66dcfacecd56</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T15:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-denies-role-in-fridge-hack-france-summons-ambassador/a-79910206--6d0355211a72.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-denies-role-in-fridge-hack-france-summons-ambassador/a-79910206?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">France has said it rules "nothing" out in response to a cyberattack on supermarket refrigeration units. Iran, however, said it categorically rejected Paris' "baseless and one-sided accusations" of IRGC involvement.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Controversial kinship: From colonial rule to the Holocaust?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5928c786253c35dfacbdafb9ba0fd02bf1288b2b586408f4b16d8b831eb8bc61</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T15:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/controversial-kinship-from-colonial-rule-to-the-holocaust/a-79902228--16129c6452e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/controversial-kinship-from-colonial-rule-to-the-holocaust/a-79902228?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hitler once called Eastern Europe "Germany's India." A new exhibition examines the links between colonialism and Nazism, and the bitter debate over where comparisons illuminate history and where they fall short.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entr