w-reports-lower-q3-earnings-as-china-woes-mount/a-79850847--9f74c40c2952.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bmw-reports-lower-q3-earnings-as-china-woes-mount/a-79850847?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">BMW reports a drop in profits in the July to September quarter amid fierce competition from China.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's celebrated children's author Janosch has died</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d55e89a31a4a56d05d863e67b285e5da64fbcf496c7d4da16d47285c4c517e1d</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T10:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-celebrated-children-s-author-janosch-has-died/a-79851600--a3fdc8a2501b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-celebrated-children-s-author-janosch-has-died/a-79851600?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bear, Tiger and Tiger-Duck: The author and illustrator Janosch achieved world fame with his heartwarming children's figures. He died at the age of 95.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Could AI give NFTs a second chance?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf6bb332456d5d357b6c49ad6754eb9f4b8aec68fb8a39d8f9ef0a310f57a1de</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T09:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/could-ai-give-nfts-a-second-chance/a-79840593--1d40731d5054.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/could-ai-give-nfts-a-second-chance/a-79840593?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">NFTs have plunged in value since their pandemic height in 2021. In some cases, they are worth 99% less than they were paid for. Yet tokenization of real-world assets and AI means the curios may yet have a future.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>From rotten food to political opponents: Researchers explore how disgust relates to our beliefs, and why the connection is complicated</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7790a680108b0d8bae4d64df2b01b7e2c4dd02587b2c8bad71c81b05358e696a</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T05:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/from-rotten-food-to-political-opponents-researchers-explore-how-disgust-relates-to-our-beliefs-and-w/a-79734659--e9b7cd7e436d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/from-rotten-food-to-political-opponents-researchers-explore-how-disgust-relates-to-our-beliefs-and-why-the-connection-is-complicated/a-79734659?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Some studies have linked disgust sensitivity to socially conservative attitudes. But does disgust shape our politics, or do our beliefs shape what we find disgusting?</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>How Berlin's Arab queers are building their community</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:daa5cdf2ddf712739e56c632e74e95f13bf464ccbec397607f43d70e1c43f3be</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T14:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-berlin-s-arab-queers-are-building-their-community/a-79833143--c676c7f349f7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-berlin-s-arab-queers-are-building-their-community/a-79833143?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the co-founder of the ADIRA Drag Festival, Lebanese performance artist, drag performer, DJ and cultural organizer Hassandra has become an essential part of Berlin's queer artistic landscape.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Football: Spanish player dies on after cardiac arrest on the pitch</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7810cd75cc9dee182ce01415fecbf9159d11af6a6f3dc3260dac6f7bb24d738a</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T11:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/football-spanish-player-dies-on-after-cardiac-arrest-on-the-pitch/a-79839398--59e3eb0d85d6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/football-spanish-player-dies-on-after-cardiac-arrest-on-the-pitch/a-79839398?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Tenerife forward Jesus de Miguel has died following a collision with the opposing goalkeeper. The Spanish second-division club has said it is "heartbroken" by the loss.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Asian Cup postponed due to Middle East conflict</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:34a75cb6f03fbf30656cee190c66f345cddc2857d35621f753a9633101f07ba4</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T11:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/asian-cup-postponed-due-to-middle-east-conflict/a-79837334--1d2a8af2e01e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/asian-cup-postponed-due-to-middle-east-conflict/a-79837334?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Asian Cup has become the latest sporting event to be affected by the ongoing conflict in the Middle East. Organizers cite "exceptional circumstances" in Saudi Arabia, which has seen several Houthi attacks of late.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Could the AI boom make borrowing more expensive in Europe?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:272659484da9447b5687ee31ff4e8925ac735cca1939ee2cab58cac27eb71c4b</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T10:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/could-the-ai-boom-make-borrowing-more-expensive-in-europe/a-79511985--c654959bd451.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/could-the-ai-boom-make-borrowing-more-expensive-in-europe/a-79511985?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">France, Germany and Italy face a volatile bond market as war inflation bites. With US tech giants now issuing billions in AI bonds, they are competing with cash-strapped European governments.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Ice hockey officials considering options after CAS order to reinstate Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f0b40eae1988759714be739240cd55bed36112bb3d38af2e6ca0e59b3431a9a8</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T15:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-officials-considering-options-after-cas-order-to-reinstate-russia/a-79831451--d3d6cb0a329c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-officials-considering-options-after-cas-order-to-reinstate-russia/a-79831451?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ice hockey's ruling body is deciding how to respond to a decision by the Court of Arbitration for Sport that allows Russia back into international competition. Germany hasn't ruled out pulling out as a tournament host.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>LA communities kick out Big Oil</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc504c6dd119218ece23fb018cf5c9c4196334d866f714dd8a14d9112d964281</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T14:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/la-communities-kick-out-big-oil/a-79830843--72df9d2c6283.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/la-communities-kick-out-big-oil/a-79830843?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After years of advocacy from residents and legal battles with Big Oil, Los Angeles voted to ban drilling and phase out oil extraction in the city. It's the first city in the United States to kick the oil industry out.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Kimi Antonelli makes history as youngest F1 champion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c77