kraine.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>The dachshund, a humorous icon with political symbolism</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:13b937bb4a2d4f2d263aeff82269d103c2dba26f2bf78ddda41e2a8fd58b6e80</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T07:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-dachshund-a-humorous-icon-with-political-symbolism/a-79640191--0ec0144d606e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-dachshund-a-humorous-icon-with-political-symbolism/a-79640191?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From Picasso to Andy Warhol, a surprising number of artists have portrayed the German breed. But the dachshund has also at times been co-opted as a political symbol.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>'Star Trek' star Patrick Stewart dies age 86</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da1c34a16215bcb33e7e08b398e27f1f6e3098564cf2c2c3e257d44eb30df270</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T22:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/star-trek-star-patrick-stewart-dies-age-86/a-79803071--53b89389ae81.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/star-trek-star-patrick-stewart-dies-age-86/a-79803071?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Shakespearean actor landed the role of a lifetime as "Star Trek" Captain Picard. He passed away at age 86.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>India increases growth forecast for fiscal year</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8460e35d4ea5d41bd70d5a1aff571a6692fca24b708858c78238dac67ca07047</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T16:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-increases-growth-forecast-for-fiscal-year/a-79798971--fa1e5ffdabbe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-increases-growth-forecast-for-fiscal-year/a-79798971?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">India's Ministry of Finance has increased its growth forecasts for the current fiscal year. But it also warned about inflation, particularly for fuel and energy, amid continued instability in the Middle East.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Volkswagen logs Q3 operating loss of €5.86 billion on Porsche writedown</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:11a7dd8b88bd4e850f2d5e7eb233f9022fbbdd3a35f4fea24b7f970ce7d584fd</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T12:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/volkswagen-logs-q3-operating-loss-of-_5-86-billion-on-porsche-writedown/a-79793796--74f8be5771cb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/volkswagen-logs-q3-operating-loss-of-€5-86-billion-on-porsche-writedown/a-79793796?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Volkswagen Group has filed its worst quarterly performance since the height of the "Dieselgate" scandal in 2015. Share prices climbed in response, however, perhaps because the bad news was so well signposted.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia shadow fleet sanctions: Can the EU act without US?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b33b9afba91b5d43fa44ea6b36a2b7b0da5d9899e73a820cbba985d55c7eb00a</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T12:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-moves-to-lift-sanctions-on-russia-s-shadow-fleet-could-undermine-western-pressure-on-moscow-and-h/a-79787035--48ad80b5a4bc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-shadow-fleet-sanctions-can-the-eu-act-without-us/a-79787035?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US is reportedly considering ways to convert "dark tankers" into legitimate vessels, allowing them to transport crude oil that is not subject to sanctions.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Can we regrow damaged seagrass meadows?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ee7fef3ef55ed0d11d69e03a7284a83ce87123a04fb91902738c07ebf325380</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T10:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-we-regrow-damaged-seagrass-meadows/a-79617925--ee57fe9c850d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-we-regrow-damaged-seagrass-meadows/a-79617925?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Seagrass protects coasts, shelters thousands of species and stores CO2. But some 30% of this valuable ecosystem has disappeared since the late 19th century. Can we bring it back?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>EU's 'Made in Europe' push unnerves global auto suppliers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:45432750df5b068f2a75a51440f68024718d48b7088c180325bf30155627d030</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T10:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-s-made-in-europe-push-unnerves-global-auto-suppliers/a-79732579--7391c1bc1a80.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-s-made-in-europe-push-unnerves-global-auto-suppliers/a-79732579?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In shielding Europe's carmakers from Chinese rivals, the EU risks hurting close partners from Turkey and Morocco to Japan and South Korea. Billions in trade and hundreds of thousands of European jobs are at stake.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>EU moves to loosen rules on pesticide use as experts sound the alarm</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4027f39c77701bf285de416f545548c09447fdcea618ee29bea25b3f114e0186</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T10:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-moves-to-loosen-rules-on-pesticide-use-as-experts-sound-the-alarm/a-79646422--0c5446a2b9ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-moves-to-loosen-rules-on-pesticide-use-as-experts-sound-the-alarm/a-79646422?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Union wants to relax rules for pesticides, saying it will be easier for farmers to adopt more environmentally friendly options. But health and environmental experts say the risks are far too great.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry></feed>
